course: dictionary
lesson: 4768
title: Housework in everyday words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Housework is the work done to keep a home clean and tidy. Cleaning, washing clothes, dusting, vacuuming and washing dishes are all housework. It is an uncountable noun, so we say "some housework", not "a housework".
explain: Read the context to check the meaning. «Mia asks whether robots will do all the housework, and Dad says, "I hope so, especially ironing."» Ironing is one of the jobs in housework, so the clues show that it means the chores at home.
explain: Notice the phrases people use with it: do the housework, help with the housework and share the housework. Each phrase tells you what people do with the chores around the home.
explain: Safety matters too. Cleaning products used in housework can be dangerous, so children use them only with an adult. When context does not give enough clues, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Housework means the work done to keep a home clean and tidy.
fact: «Housework» is uncountable, so you say «some housework» and not «a housework».
fact: Examples of housework are cleaning, washing clothes, dusting, vacuuming and washing dishes.
fact: Children can help with housework, such as making beds, setting the table and tidying their rooms.
fact: Cleaning products used in housework can be dangerous, so children use them only with an adult.
exercise: «Mia asks whether robots will do all the housework.» What is housework? | *Work done to keep a home clean and tidy | Work done in a factory | Games played indoors | Shopping for food in a big town
exercise: Which of these is housework? | *Washing the dishes | Driving to the sea | Reading a comic in bed | Painting a portrait
exercise: What does «share the housework» mean? | Nobody has to do any chores | *Everyone in the home does some of the chores | Only one person does every chore | Chores are sold to the neighbours
test: Why should children use cleaning products only with an adult? | Because they smell nice to adults | *Because cleaning products can be dangerous | Because they are only for the garden | Because they are always free
test: «Much housework is invisible, like booking appointments and planning meals.» Which of these is an example of invisible housework? | Mowing the lawn | *Booking appointments | Painting the fence | Washing the car
exam: Which sentence uses housework correctly? | We need to share houseworks at home | We need to share housework's at home | We need to share a housework at home | *We need to share the housework at home
